# Signing up to Island Hop, and verifying the email with the code the app sends.
# The app's email goes to HumanTest's test mailbox ("email" in humantest.config.json), never out;
# the addresses are on .test, a domain that can't receive email anyway.
# The account is made by a phrase (e2e/phrases/accounts.ht) and deleted again when the test ends.

Test: A new traveller verifies their email with the code they get

  Given new traveller signs up as "traveller.{unique}@humantest.test"

  As new traveller:
    "traveller.{unique}@humantest.test" should get an email "Verify Your Email"
    the email should contain "This code will expire in 15 minutes"
    the email should not contain "Test@12345"
    remember the code in the email as otp
    should still be on "/verify-email"
    # Six digits send the code by themselves; there is nothing to click.
    type "{otp}" in "Verification code"
    backend should receive POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email
    backend should reply 200 OK
    should see "Email Verified!"


Test: A wrong code doesn't verify the email

  Given new traveller signs up as "traveller.{unique}@humantest.test"

  As new traveller:
    "traveller.{unique}@humantest.test" should get an email "Verify Your Email"
    type "000000" in "Verification code"
    backend should receive POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email
    backend should reply 400 Bad Request
    should see "Invalid email or OTP"
    should not see "Email Verified!"
